From 6ba4d6d77fae5adf3bc67fa5c32cb5faccb06dd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pbs05 <27010143+pbs05@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:10:06 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] net: pcs: airoha: add AN7581 PON line modes

Rebased from patches-6.18 onto linux-7.3.1 + patches-7.3.

AN7581 PON support is included. The AN7583 PCS sections are omitted:
the AN7583 PCS driver (604-01) is not part of patches-7.3, so its
referenced functions do not exist. Bringing AN7583 back requires
rebasing 604-01 first.

Hunks ported manually against the rewritten PCS driver:
- pcs-airoha-common.c: PON API block inserted before
  airoha_pcs_init_usxgmii(); 6.18 context line
  'const struct airoha_pcs_match_data *data = priv->data;' no longer
  matches (7.3 uses maps-based lookup).
  The an7581_pcs_pon match_data already existed in 7.3 and gained the
  PON entry points via git apply; the an7583_pcs_pon match_data hunk
  was dropped (no AN7583 PCS driver in 7.3).
- pcs-airoha.h: RX_FLL_3 / TX_CALIB_1 / pon_mode / match_data pointer
  additions inserted at register-appropriate offsets; 7.3 removed the
  TX_CALIB_0 block, so TX_CALIB_1 was placed after the 0x260 TX_RST_B
  block instead.
- pcs-an7581.c: include hunk placed after the SPDX comment (7.3
  dropped linux/math.h).
- include/linux/pcs/pcs-airoha.h: new file, applied cleanly.

